<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How the neosh website and application handle your data."
  updated="August 23, 2026"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not collect personal data. There are no accounts, no cookies, no analytics
    and no tracking. The neosh application runs entirely on your own computer, and your
    conversations, files and API keys stay there.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>When you visit this site, your browser makes a few requests to third parties:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Fonts</strong> are loaded from Google Fonts. Google receives your IP address as part
      of serving them. See the
      <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The star count</strong> in the navigation is fetched from the GitHub API. GitHub
      receives your IP address as part of that request. See the
      <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider may keep standard server logs, such as IP addresses and request times, to
    operate and secure the service. We do not use them to identify visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>The neosh application</h2>
  <p>
    neosh is software you install and run locally. We do not operate servers that see your data,
    and the application sends no telemetry.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your conversations and files are stored on your own machine.</li>
    <li>
      API keys and credentials are read at request time and are never written to disk in plaintext
      or included in logs.
    </li>
    <li>
      When you use an AI provider, neosh connects to it directly with the account you configured.
      What that provider does with your requests is governed by its own privacy policy.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Since we do not collect or store personal data, there is nothing for us to hand over, correct
    or delete. If you believe something on this page is wrong or incomplete, please
    <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://github.com/neoswarm/neosh/issues">open an issue on GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page with an updated date.
  </p>
</Legal>
